  "The English teen edition quotes the ASV in each epigraph; every French epigraph is Louis Segond (1910) verbatim (whole verse or the same partial span as the English), with the “(ASV)” label dropped and only French spacing before : ; ? ! added. Psalm 81:10 (English) is Psaume 81:11 in Segond and is cited that way.",
  "Segond has no word for KJV/ASV “wide” in Psalm 81:10, so Hyde's repeated “Wide, Lord” prayer (ch. 8) is « Toute grande, Seigneur », matching the shipped children's edition; that and the other re-personed or paraphrased echoes (Hebrews 12:1 « le péché qui m’enveloppait si facilement », Zechariah 2:8 « la prunelle de mon œil », Revelation 12:10 « accusateur des frères », Philippians 4:8 with an ellipsis, Proverbs 27:6) are self_rendered.",
